						"boxes" : [ 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-28",
									"linecount" : 3,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 444.0, 566.0, 47.0 ],
									"text" : "Moving forward through questions sets the ordered tracks in a [Umenu] according to each question group. (0-6) (7-13) (14-20), etc. The audio plays when participants clic the associated labels [test sample] [a] [b]... and so on, for each block."
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-27",
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 1370.0, 566.0, 20.0 ]
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-21",
									"linecount" : 2,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 631.0, 566.0, 33.0 ],
									"text" : "If more questions, multiple choices answers and message boxes are added, the trackbar can be synchronized by adjusting the letters or values in the [sel] object in the main patcher"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-20",
									"linecount" : 4,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 747.0, 566.0, 60.0 ],
									"text" : "Participants can navigate the test using the \"Next Question or \"Previous Question\" message boxes. One can return to skipped questions using the bottom \"track bar\" which shows a green label after each question is answered, or is left blank if a question is unanswered. One can register skipped or missed questions and/or return to modify answers if necessary."
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-17",
									"linecount" : 3,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 391.0, 566.0, 47.0 ],
									"text" : "Currently only .aif  files are directed to the patch from the folder. This can be changed inside the [Audio-Player] sub patch from the message box [types AIFF] to either [types Wav] or [types FLAC] to accomodates other lossless audio formats such as .wave and .flac"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-16",
									"linecount" : 34,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 861.0, 566.0, 476.0 ],
									"text" : "The text in the [Block_text] Subpatch is ordered in two Parts, the first being the first fours blocks and the second being the fifth.\n\nThis is ordered by block using the [split] object which groups the blocks in a series of 8 questions. On the 9th, the block indication at the top centre of the display screen changes i.e. : from \"block 1\" to \"block 2\" etc. The display grouping can be changed via the numbers in the [split] objects.\n\nThe first four blocks display questions:\n\n[Test Sample] [A] [B] [C] [D] [E]    \n\nand answers:\n\n[A] [B] [C] [D] [E]     \n\nWhen participants reach question 33, the labels change from the above-mentionned to :\n\n[A-B] [A-C] [A-D] [B-C] [B-D] [C-D]\n\nand :\n\n[A] [B] [C] [D] [E] [F]\n\nThe displayed text can be changed in the [Block_text] subpatch via the message boxes.\nThe directions and question texts can be changed via the message boxes on the right of the same sub patch.\n\nThe X/Y position of the message boxes in presentation mode can be changed via the subpatches [setting 1] and [setting 2] found in the main patch. This is done by copy-pasting the X/Y coordinates found in the inspector under \"presentation rectangle\" and changing them in the [setting 1] or [setting 2] sub patches message boxes, labelled from 1 to 6.\n\n At block 5, an additionnal [F] answer box is made visible. The occurrence for this change (at question 33) can be modified via the [Block_text] subpatch.\n"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"fontface" : 1,
									"fontsize" : 16.0,
									"id" : "obj-15",
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 821.0, 282.0, 24.0 ],
									"text" : "Text"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-14",
									"linecount" : 6,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 537.0, 566.0, 87.0 ],
									"text" : "In it's current state, the patch contains 41 questions. Each question is a group composed of 6 tracks linked to 6 multiple choice answers. It is possible to change the number of questions and track grouping in the [Questions] subpatch. The amount of questions can be changed through the last value in the [counter] object. This will automatically change the display and all associated with this numbering. The amount of variables in each group can be modified from the number \"6\" to the desired variable in the expression box [expr $i1 * 6 + 1]"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"fontface" : 1,
									"fontsize" : 16.0,
									"id" : "obj-12",
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 504.0, 282.0, 24.0 ],
									"text" : "Questions and Groupings"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"fontface" : 1,
									"fontsize" : 16.0,
									"id" : "obj-11",
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 311.0, 282.0, 24.0 ],
									"text" : "Audio, Format and  Playback"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-10",
									"linecount" : 4,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 676.0, 566.0, 60.0 ],
									"text" : "The participant's name has to be written in the box shown in presentation mode to enable the \"Save\" command. Each answer saves automatically as the participant proceeds through the questionnaire. The answers can be found in a \"participantname\" .json file in the same folder as the patch. If the \"Next Question\" is clicked beforehand, the \"file path\" option will be prompted. "
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-9",
									"linecount" : 2,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 348.0, 566.0, 33.0 ],
									"text" : "If the Audio files are in the same folder as the patch, the audio will autogenerates at the opening of the patch. Clicking the initialize button will run through the list and enable playback."
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-5",
									"linecount" : 14,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 19.0, 99.0, 566.0, 194.0 ],
									"text" : "The test is ordered to accommodate the stimulus in groups of 6, starting from the first \"test sample\" through the questionnaire. Question one generates Test Sample 1 and the following five stimuli.\ni.e. :\n\nStimulus 0 (Test sample 1) : Stimulus 1 (a), Stimulus 2 (b), Stimulus 3 (c), Stimulus 4 (d), Stimulus 5 (e)\n\nStimulus 6 (Test sample 1) : Stumulus 7 (a), stimulus 8 (b), stimulus 9 (c), stimulus 10 (d), stimulus 11 (e)\n\netc.\n\nThis pattern is the same for all the blocks but the labels and figuration in block 5 are modified. They are still in groups of 6.\n\nQuestion 0 is blank"
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
